 <section data-page="1" class="learn-page cover-page"><div class="book-cover-art"><img src={`${base}/art/cards/heaven-background.webp`} alt="Golden gates opening into a luminous heaven."/></div><div class="cover-lettering"><p class="eyebrow">2–5 PLAYERS · THREE ROUNDS · ILLUSTRATED RULEBOOK</p><h1>Higher<br/><em>Powers</em></h1><p class="book-subtitle">A game of divine organization,<br/>ambitious angels, and heavenly bureaucracy.</p></div><div class="cover-bottom"><p>Heaven is overflowing. Twelve angels have been asked to restore order.<br/>Unfortunately, only one gets promoted.</p><p class="eyebrow">BRING YOUR RUMMIKUB TILES. WE’LL BRING THE MIRACLES.</p></div></section>
 <section data-page="2" class="learn-page"><p class="eyebrow">WELCOME TO THE GRAND ORDER</p><h2>A place for every soul.</h2><p class="lead">Empty your hand first. Keep your score high. Expect divine interference.</p><div class="book-two-col"><div><h3>Set the table</h3><ol><li>Bring 106 Rummikub tiles, racks, and an opaque bag. Numbered tiles are souls; the two jokers are wild.</li><li>Deal two random Angels to each player. Choose one each, reveal choices together, and set the others aside. Keep your chosen Angel all game.</li><li>Mix all souls and deal fourteen to each player. The rest stay in the bag.</li><li>Reset Favor to zero and turn powers upright. Choose a random first starter; play clockwise.</li><li>Reveal an ordinary Decree for round one. Use a different ordinary Decree for round two, and one Final Judgment for round three.</li></ol></div><figure class="book-card"><GameCard card={angels[0]}/><figcaption>Your Angel grants one miracle each round.</figcaption></figure></div><div class="three-principles"><div><b>Organize</b><p>Build legal formations in Heaven.</p></div><div><b>Invoke</b><p>Use your once-per-round power.</p></div><div><b>Deliver</b><p>Empty your hand to end the round.</p></div></div><aside class="book-note">No 30-point minimum. Each round, first meld a complete legal formation from your own hand. You may then extend and rearrange Heaven in that same turn. Bring coins for Favor and pencils for scores.</aside></section>
 <section data-page="3" class="learn-page"><p class="eyebrow">LEARN THE SHAPE OF HEAVEN</p><h2>Two kinds of order.</h2><p>Each soul in Heaven belongs to one legal formation. After your opening meld, the shared table is yours to rearrange on your turn, except for another Angel’s Sanctuary.</p><div class="formation-example"><div><h3>A Choir</h3><p>Three or four souls of one rank, each a different color.</p></div><div class="tile-line"><Tile rank={7} color="red"/><Tile rank={7}/><Tile rank={7} color="black"/></div></div><div class="formation-example"><div><h3>A Procession</h3><p>Three or more consecutive ranks in one color.</p></div><div class="tile-line"><Tile rank={4}/><Tile rank={5}/><Tile rank={6}/><Tile rank={7}/></div></div><h3>Move the fourth. Keep the three.</h3><p>Once you have opened, a four-tile Choir can lend its fourth soul to another formation, leaving a legal Choir behind. You may split, combine, and rebuild formations, as long as all of Heaven is legal when your action ends.</p><div class="tile-demo"><div class="tile-line"><Tile rank={7} color="red"/><Tile rank={7}/><Tile rank={7} color="black"/><span class="moving-tile"><Tile rank={7} color="gold"/></span></div><span class="demo-label">The gold 7 joins a gold 5–6 to make a new Procession.</span><div class="tile-line"><Tile rank={5} color="gold"/><Tile rank={6} color="gold"/><Tile rank={7} color="gold"/></div></div><aside class="book-note"><strong>God may disagree.</strong> The active Decree changes the affected formation rules. Read it before planning your turn. Round three restores ordinary formations.</aside></section>
 <section data-page="4" class="learn-page"><p class="eyebrow">YOUR TURN IN HEAVEN</p><h2>Make a contribution.<br/>Or ask for guidance.</h2><div class="book-two-col"><div><h3>Organize</h3><p>Each round, first meld one complete legal formation from your own hand. After that, you may extend or rearrange Heaven, including on that same turn. Finish every formation legally. Organizing powers do not waive the opening requirement.</p><h3>Or draw</h3><p>Your Favor determines how many random bag souls you may inspect. Keep one and return and mix the rest. Drawing ends your turn. You may draw even if you could play.</p><h3>Favor rewards delivery</h3><p>Deliver souls from your hand to earn Favor: add three souls, gain three Favor. Rearranging alone earns none.</p></div><div><figure class="book-card"><GameCard card={decrees[3]}/><figcaption>Candy Cane requires alternating colors in every Procession.</figcaption></figure></div></div><h3>More Favor, more choice</h3>
<p>Compare everyone’s Favor before drawing. With no ties, the leader may inspect as many souls as there are players. Each place below the leader inspects one fewer, down to one for last place. You still keep only one.</p><table class="example-table"><thead><tr><th>Four players’ Favor</th><th>6</th><th>4</th><th>2</th><th>0</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Souls inspected</th><td>4</td><td>3</td><td>2</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Ties take the lower allowance.</strong> If two players tie for first in a four-player game, both inspect three souls. Favor totals of 5, 5, 2, 0 give allowances of 3, 3, 2, 1. If everyone is tied, everyone inspects one.</p>
<aside class="book-note">Your Angel’s card tells you when to use its once-per-round power. Turn it sideways when spent.</aside></section>
 <section data-page="5" class="learn-page"><p class="eyebrow">MIRACLES, REGIONS & THE FINAL JUDGMENT</p><h2>The table tells the story.</h2><div class="book-two-col"><div><h3>Sanctuary</h3><p>Everything inside is protected. Additions become protected; removed souls become public. You may leave a legal three-tile Choir safe while using its fourth tile elsewhere.</p><h3>Purgatory</h3><p>Raphael may place one excess table soul here during hand play. Purgatory does not prevent going out. On later turns, rescue into a Procession or draw.</p><h3>Scales commitments</h3><p>Keep chosen tiles separate on your rack. Delivery earns an immediate, permanent printed-rank credit. Once delivered, a committed tile is ordinary. No tile history is recorded.</p></div><figure class="book-card"><GameCard card={judgments[2]}/><figcaption>Round three brings one of five catch-up judgments.</figcaption></figure></div><h3>An empty hand ends the round</h3><p>Complete the action, then check for an empty hand. Other players lose the value of their undelivered souls, including Purgatory; jokers cost 30. The winner gains the sum of those penalties.</p><div class="score-example"><div><b>+20</b><span>WINNER</span></div><div><b>−8</b><span>SECOND PLAYER</span></div><div><b>−12</b><span>THIRD PLAYER</span></div></div><aside class="book-note">Apply the current Final Judgment, then add round scores. After three rounds, the highest total wins. The following reference contains every power, decree, scoring rule, and exception.</aside></section>
